mos3_ac: F27 (R94): one sp_mos3 NMOS in saturation (vgs 1.5, vds 3, vbs -0.5), its gate driven at 1, 1.5 and 2 kHz: VACASK's small-signal gm is the derivative of the DC law, ngspice-45 level 3's is not; DC agrees, the drain current at 1 kHz does not (families/mos3/nom_sat_acg_1k)
load "spice/mos3.osdi"
model vs vsource
model nm sp_mos3 type=1 vto=0.7 kp=1e-4 gamma=0.5 phi=0.7 nsub=1e16 vmax=5e4 xj=0.5u nfs=1e11 theta=0.05 eta=0.1 kappa=0.2 delta=0.5 ld=0.1u tox=20n cgso=3e-10 cgdo=3e-10 cgbo=2e-10 cj=5e-4 mj=0.5 cjsw=2e-10 mjsw=0.33 pb=0.8 js=1e-4 fc=0.5 rd=10 rs=10
vd (d 0) vs dc=3.0
vg (g 0) vs dc=1.5 mag=1
vb (b 0) vs dc=-0.5
m1 (d g 0 b) nm w=10u l=2u ad=20p as=20p pd=24u ps=24u
control
  analysis ac1 ac from=1e3 to=2e3 mode="lin" points=2
endc
